---
// The five tones, each with the words the app actually says.
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
---
<ol class="tones">
  <li>
    <span class="dot green"></span>
    <div>
      <p class="say">13 of 13 answering</p>
      <p class="mean"><b>Green</b> is done, available, healthy. It stays quiet, because healthy is the normal state.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li class="fault">
    <Icon name="warn" size={20} class="tone-amber" />
    <div>
      <p class="say">Charge is stuck at 47% <span class="tone-amber">· nothing for 3 h</span></p>
      <p class="mean"><b>Amber</b> is a fault, and only a fault. It always comes with the way out.</p>
      <span class="remedy">Try another download</span>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="dot red"></span>
    <div>
      <p class="say tone-red">Radarr did not answer since 20:41</p>
      <p class="mean"><b>Red</b> means nothing replied at the address. Nothing else is ever red, not even a delete.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="dot blue"></span>
    <div>
      <p class="say tone-blue">Downloading 62% · ready around 21:40</p>
      <p class="mean"><b>Blue</b> is on its way, or waiting on someone.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="dot neutral"></span>
    <div>
      <p class="say">Not out yet</p>
      <p class="mean"><b>Neutral</b> is the backlog. Something missing or wanted is the resting state of a media stack, not damage.</p>
    </div>
  </li>
</ol>

<style>
  .tones {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-radius: var(--r-slab);
    background: rgb(18 18 24 / 0.82);
    border: 1px solid var(--hair);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 22px 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 20px 24px;
  }
  li + li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  li > :global(svg) {
    transform: translateY(4px);
  }
  li > .dot {
    margin-left: 6px;
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .say {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .mean {
    margin-top: 4px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .mean b {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .remedy {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 40px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding: 0 16px;
    border-radius: var(--r-control);
    background: var(--amber);
    color: var(--amber-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .fault {
    background: var(--amber-wash);
  }
</style>
